def representation():
 rows=load(OUT/'representation_HDFS.json')+load(OUT/'representation_BGL.json');base=[z for z in rows if not z['budget']];tab=[];recovery=[]
 for z in base:
  q=z['string_partition'];sq=z['sequence'];lx=z['test_lexical'];tab.append([z['system'],z['parser'],q['predicted_groups'],f"{q['ARI']:.7f}",f"{q['NMI']:.5f}",f"{q['pair_precision']:.7f}/{q['pair_recall']:.7f}",f"{q['event_macro_split_fraction']:.3f}",f"{sq['one_to_one_changed_positions']:.5f}",f"{lx['word_cosine']:.5f}"])
 for system in ('HDFS','BGL'):
  for name in ('llama/cache','llama/strong','llama/AdaParser','gemma/cache','gemma/strong','gemma/AdaParser'):
   for method in ('frequent','dsize','usize','U-zero x size','U+V5-zero x size','oracle'):
    z=[r for r in rows if r['system']==system and r['parser']==name and r['method']==method and r['budget']==20]
    if z:recovery.append([system,name,method,f"{np.mean([r['actual_reviews'] for r in z]):.1f}",f"{np.mean([r['corrected_lines'] for r in z]):.1f}",f"{np.mean([r['changed_template_groups'] for r in z]):.1f}",f"{np.mean([r['test_lexical']['word_cosine'] for r in z]):.5f}",f"{np.mean([r['sequence']['one_to_one_changed_positions'] for r in z]):.5f}"])
 write('parsing_representation_impact.md',[
 '# Parsing representation impact',
 'Executed984 baseline/review rows, reusing stored assignments and rankings; no model generation or predictor refit. Grouping statistics use all50,000 matched lines/system. Sequence diagnostics use the old frozen complete units (39 anomalous HDFS blocks/116 positions;2,500 BGL windows/50,000 positions). Lexical results below are test-only (24 HDFS blocks;500 all-normal BGL windows). These are invalid anomaly-recovery populations but usable explicitly conditional representation diagnostics. No detector harm is inferred.',
 '## Grouping, event sequences and lexical features',table(['System','Parser','String events','ARI','NMI','Pair P/R','GT-event split fraction','One-to-one changed positions','Test word cosine'],tab),
 'Partition metrics use contingency counts rather than quadratic pairs. Machine-readable outputs also include merged/split event counts, affected line frequencies, GT-event completeness and predicted-event purity (event macro means), plus line-weighted measures. None outputs are explicitly observed parsing failures; they form a diagnostic failure event, not missing predictions. Drain/base/strong operational IDs are kept separately from final-template-string event partitions. AdaParser uses actual final assignments, verified bijective to strings by the prior200,000 CSV joins.',
 'IDs are never compared numerically. We report two diagnostic GT-informed mappings: majority-GT mapping (many-to-one, deliberately collapses splits) and maximum-weight one-to-one matching (Hungarian contingency assignment), retaining unmatched predicted events as distinct symbols. Unmatched/ambiguous/tied event counts and affected positions are saved. Both use GT across the matched prefix solely for representation comparison, never to construct a deployable detector. Sequence unigram/bigram/3-gram JS divergence is in bits; bigrams measure transition joint distributions. Edges never cross unit boundaries. Majority mapping alone would hide AdaParser over-splitting, so it is not the sole distortion measure.',
 'HDFS AdaParser is identical to GT. BGL AdaParser has no mixed-GT final groups but splits2/54 GT types, affecting222 lines; Llama has66 final groups and Gemma57 vs54 GT. This is real partition change that event/context detectors can observe, although ARI is near1 and majority-mapped sequence changes are zero. Drain/cache have almost identical partitions despite much worse strict text accuracy. Neither high ARI nor a zero majority-mapped difference proves harmlessness.',
 'Word and character3–5-gram TF-IDF share a single frozen vocabulary/IDF per system, fit on the union of unique training templates across conditions including GT (diagnostic only). Validation/test text is transformed without fitting. Token bags use lowercase[a-z]+ with wildcards removed. Saved measures include constant-token multiset loss/addition, token-frequency JS, vocabulary loss/introduction, word/character cosine, GT-event macro cosine, and rare(≤20 prefix lines)/frequent stratification. This is lexical preservation, not semantic correctness. Empty/out-of-vocabulary GT vectors are counted; a both-empty cosine convention of1 is explicit and must not be read as semantic agreement.',
 '## Stored review replay',table(['System','Parser','Order','Reviews≤20','Newly correct lines','Changed output groups','Test word cosine','Mapped sequence change'],recovery),
 'Full budgets5/10/20/50 and five seeds are in representation_{HDFS,BGL}.json. “Changed output groups” counts reviewed operational groups whose output string changes; it is not a claim that every member becomes correct. Oracle uses saved line-gain ordering, not a newly optimized lexical oracle. U/zero-target histories are included where stored; static Clotho rankings and real-AdaParser U are unavailable. Strong uses final C2 templates, including its verified seeds; no greedy substitute.',
 'Newly wrong lines and net correct-line changes are saved separately; a majority-template intervention may sacrifice previously correct minority members. Operational membership grouping metrics are exactly invariant under every template-only review. Corrected text can coalesce string-derived event IDs, so the separately reported string partition/sequence can change; mixed groups cannot be split by this intervention. There are no stored grouping-aware human repairs. Calling the operational ARI improvement positive would be incorrect.',
 'At BGL20 reviews, frequency and D restore the same test lexical cosine for both base caches and both AdaParsers, despite differing whole-stream wrong-line recovery. Both AdaParsers reach numerical cosine1 on this all-normal test. Frequency and D therefore do not demonstrate distinct recovered lexical information here. Effects on rarer templates/whole-stream group counts can differ; the cost analysis treats those as separate outcomes.',
 '## Error-type integration and implications',
 'The completed severity audit is reused: BGL Llama AdaParser primary proxies48 exact/12 nonmatching representation/5 variable extraction/1 uncertain; Gemma50/2/4/1. These are first-line automatic proxies, not independently verified semantic error labels. Variable-boundary and word proxies can change token bags without changing operational membership. High-frequency errors weight line-level lexical distortion more heavily by construction; event-macro and rare/frequent fields expose this weighting rather than assuming rare errors are less important. The stored217-example blinded semantic worksheet still lacks independent annotation; no new heuristic semantic facts are assigned.',
 'For cached parsers, a semantic/text-sensitive detector has more representation headroom than fixed-group count models. For real BGL AdaParser, over-splitting provides sequence/context headroom while text distortion is small on the stored test. Broader valid matched outputs are absent, and strong detector health is unmeasured. Lexical changes, grouping changes and anomaly recovery remain three different claims.',
 '[Four-panel PDF](../results_phase3/cpu_research/representation.pdf) shows ARI/NMI, one-to-one sequence changes, line-weighted lexical distributions and budget recovery. Scripts/results remain separate from validated earlier paper plots.'])

def costs():
 rr=load(OUT/'review_cost_points.json');front=load(OUT/'review_cost_frontiers.json');cc=load(OUT/'review_cost_comparisons.json');pp=load(OUT/'review_cost_pareto.json');tab=[]
 for z in cc:
  if z['cohort']=='all' and z['scenario']=='A_target' and z['review_to_label_cost']==1 and z['parser']=='base' and z['metric'] in ('lines','groups') and z['method'] in ('D × size','U+V5 × size','U-zero × size') and z['budget_review_equivalents'] in (20,100,150):
   lo,hi=z['system_cluster_CI95'];tab.append([z['model'],z['budget_review_equivalents'],z['metric'],z['method'],len(z['systems']),f"{z['mean_delta']:+.4f}",f'[{lo:+.4f},{hi:+.4f}]',f"{z['paired_system_win_probability']:.2f}"])
 amort=[]
 for z in cc:
  if z['cohort']=='all' and z['scenario']=='B_amortized' and z['review_to_label_cost']==10 and z['parser']=='base' and z['metric']=='lines' and z['budget_review_equivalents']==100 and z['method'] in ('D × size','U+V5 × size','U-zero × size'):
   amort.append([z['model'],z['method'],f"{z['mean_delta']:+.4f}",str([round(x,4) for x in z['system_cluster_CI95']])])
 # Long-form CSV is the per-system table, keeping seeds/conditions separate.
 with (OUT/'review_cost_per_system.csv').open('w') as f:
  fields=list(rr[0]);w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=fields);w.writeheader();w.writerows(rr)
 dom=Counter((p['model'],p['parser'],p['scenario'],p['method']) for p in pp if p['dominated_by'])
 write('review_cost_analysis.md',[
 '# Review budget and label cost analysis',
 f'New analysis of{len(rr):,} stored outcomes: actual label counts, source acquisition/amortization and variable-cost frontiers. Existing equal-effort experiments were reused, not rerun. Base, strong, real AdaParser and residual-tail populations remain distinct. No rankings or hyperparameters changed; no curves were interpolated.',
 '## Label-count audit',table(['Method','Real target labels','Source labels per target','Synthetic/examples and online feedback'],[
 ['Frequency / Random / consistency','0','0','Review actions only'],['Clotho reference100','90','0','10 synthetic tests; static stream rankings unavailable'],['U+V5 stream','90','6000 Llama /5500 Gemma','10 synthetic tests excluded from fitting; review feedback reused'],['D','0 deployment warm-start','6000 /5500','Other systems:500 labelled inputs each; feedback refits'],['U-zero / U+V5-zero','0 deployment warm-start','6000 /5500','Source-only U model plus review feedback'],['Strong parser (common)','10 verified templates','0','Common to every strategy in that parser setting'],['Real AdaParser (common)','32 labelled candidates','0','Common to every strategy; distinct from predictor labels']]),
 'Counts audited in source_data/source_ds/suite_ref and the stored reference100 protocol. Source labels are real capped-suite input labels, not nominal reference sizes. Source weights0.1/1 or repeated online weights do not create additional unique human acquisitions. The existing strong/base usize histories are the frozen U+V5 stream setting, not U-alone. U-alone and static Clotho review curves cannot be invented from capped-suite AUCs. Zero-target U is available for caches, not real AdaParser.',
 'A “binary label” here is one hypothetical human correctness judgement per labelled input, although the experiment actually obtains PASS labels from stored generations/GT. Auditing five outputs might cost more than a single judgement; no measured human timings exist. We do not count machine-generated sample counts as five independent human labels. Synthetic tests, parser candidates, anomaly labels and review corrections are different resources. The32 AdaParser candidates are common existing template supervision; their original labelling effort is treated as32 review equivalents, and strong seeds as10. Sensitivity of this common cost shifts the budget axis without changing matched policy rankings.',
 '## Cost definitions',
 'Scenario A counts target labels plus online reviews; source acquisition is disclosed separately. Scenario B single deployment also charges all source labels (6000/5500). Scenario B amortized acquires a union of6500/6000 source-labelled inputs once for deployment to13/12 systems:500 per system; it does not charge each leave-one-out source pool again. This is an analytical portfolio scenario, not a new multi-system experiment. Labels can be reused across base/strong episodes of the same model; no cross-model or cross-parser correctness-label reuse is assumed. Further repeated-episode amortization is possible but not measured here.',
 'For review/binary-label cost ratio r∈{1,5,10}, cost in review equivalents = common parser template reviews + online reviews + (target labels + scenario-specific source labels)/r. A reviewed item supplies its feedback label once; refitting or repeating its weight is not charged again. Tail analyses include the20 prior frequency reviews once before additional tail reviews. No dollars, GPU seconds or binary labels are added without a stated conversion.',
 'Budgets20/50/100/150/200 select the largest actually stored affordable review depth, independently of outcomes. Stored full histories support5/10/20/50/100; zero-target histories and real-parser histories stop at50 or queue exhaustion. Thus some methods leave budget unused. These are measured attainable frontiers, not extrapolated optimal curves; especially a50-vs100-depth comparison cannot establish that a zero-target method would still lose if its missing100-review curve were run. Exhausted queues cost only actual reviews. Real AdaParser has no stored reviewed FTA, so it is unavailable rather than filled with another parser’s metric.',
 '## Paired target-effort results',table(['Model','Budget','Outcome','Method − frequency','Systems','Mean delta','System-cluster95%CI','System win probability'],tab),
 'At100 target review equivalents and r=1, U+V5 can afford only10 stored reviews after90 real labels; frequency can afford100 (subject to exhaustion). Its wrong-line fraction deficit is0.1600 Llama and0.1177 Gemma. At150, U+V5 reaches its50-review point and the deficits shrink to0.0380/0.0291. This corrects the old nominal100-label/capped120-review comparison. No downstream detector improvement is inferred.',
 'At20 target review equivalents, U-zero’s base-parser wrong-line gain is approximately zero, while wrong-group gains are+0.0321 Llama/+0.0378 Gemma. It avoids90 target labels and can help template coverage at small budgets, conditional on existing source supervision. This is a narrower operational advantage than generally improving corrected line volume.',
 '## Total-label and variable-cost sensitivity',table(['Model','Method','Δ wrong-line fraction vs frequency','System-cluster95%CI'],amort),
 'This table uses amortized source costs, r=10 and100 review-equivalent budget; source-dependent methods remain below frequency on base-parser line recovery in these supported curves. Single-deployment source methods cannot reach even their first measured point within20–200 review equivalents under r≤10 because5500/6000 source labels already cost550/600 reviews at r=10. “Zero target” does not mean zero total acquisition cost. With source labels treated as sunk, A is the relevant incremental deployment scenario.',
 '## Statistics, Pareto and coverage',
 table(['Model','Scenario','Method','Dominated by (all included objectives)'],[[p['model'],p['scenario'],p['method'],', '.join(p['dominated_by']) or 'Nondominated'] for p in pp if p['parser']=='base' and p['budget']==150 and p['ratio']==1 and p['scenario'] in ('A_target','B_single','B_amortized')]),
 'Five seeds are matched within system; outcomes are averaged within system before4000 system-cluster bootstrap draws (seed20261111). Paired seed macros, per-system deltas,95% intervals and paired system win probability (ties count½) are saved. Deterministic seed duplicates are not five independent populations. Held-out comparisons excluding HDFS/Spark/Linux are saved separately as cohort=held_out; all-system tables include tuning systems and are descriptive. “Zero target” refers to deployment fitting: the research tuning systems were previously labelled. Held-out systems provide the cleaner zero-target evidence. Scenario B source pools include the tuning systems for held-out deployments; no extra tuning labels are charged twice.',
 'Pareto comparisons use exactly common systems at each model/parser/scenario/budget, minimizing actual human cost and maximizing all jointly available outcomes (wrong lines, wrong groups, FTA). A method is marked dominated only if another is no worse on every included objective and strictly better on at least one. Source/GPU costs are never silently combined. These are descriptive point frontiers, not uncertainty-adjusted dominance claims. A method can lose on lines and remain nondominated through group/FTA recovery; no universal winner is claimed. Full dominated_by/objective fields are in review_cost_pareto.json.',
 'Coverage: Llama cached analyses11 systems (pre-restoration R2/R3 histories omit HDFS/OpenSSH), Gemma12; real AdaParser12 each, with Llama Mac excluded. No reconstitution of missing adaptive histories was attempted. Perfect-system wrong-line/group fractions are undefined and jointly excluded per metric, so metric cohorts can differ. Real-parser32-candidate costs are included: budget50 generally reaches10 stored online reviews, not20. Per-system seed outcomes are in review_cost_per_system.csv; full/tail remain separately named parser populations.',
 'GPU/inference measurements from log_parsing_cost_quality.md describe capped-suite scoring and cannot reliably price D’s different layer/prompt or AdaParser’s correction calls. They are not converted into invented deployment GPU cost or dollar axes. Existing parser call/token/wall measurements remain in adaparser_e2e_details.md; no new GPU inference was measured.',
 '[Paper-ready four-panel PDF](../results_phase3/cpu_research/review_cost.pdf): supported performance/effort curves, amortized label cost, descriptive Pareto points and explicitly hypothetical cost-ratio sensitivity. Connecting lines guide the eye only; comparisons use measured points. Frontiers/paired comparisons/coverage/Pareto records are in results_phase3/cpu_research/.'])

def pilot():
 write('gpu_pilot_plan.md',[
 '# Frozen next GPU pilot',
 'The smallest executable next step is a GT-only detector health pilot, not a matched parser recovery claim. Full-horizon matched parser outputs do not exist; do not train a recovery comparison on the old prefix. Decisions are frozen in configs/cpu_gpu_pilot.json and full_horizon split manifests. No GPU job ran in this CPU task.',
 '## Data and conditions',
 'Initial dataset BGL, full raw-line60/20/20 chronological cuts, nonoverlapping20-line any-alert windows; purge2 crossings and retain the final short unit with explicit within-unit left padding for its DeepLog context. All46312 validation/46313 test units are retained; train10000 normal units chosen by lowest SHA256(unit ID). HDFS prepared as a GT control with complete contained blocks and10000 normal training blocks; no shared raw lines across splits. Training vocabulary only; explicit UNK0 and contextual mask token at vocab+1. No test labels select vocabulary, units, rankings or hyperparameters. Both datasets’ exact IDs/input hashes are saved.',
 'After GT health, obtain GT/Drain/base/strong/real-AdaParser assignments on identical frozen units. Predicted prepare requires a complete JSON map original LineId→actual event assignment; missing rows fail with the first missing ID. No GT fill. Template strings for semantic work need a matching event→text table; original IDs and final-vs-temporal assignment provenance must be retained. Parser seed candidates/overlap and adaptation need explicit new control, because current whole-prefix final outputs are transductive relative to detector splits.',
 '## Detectors and frozen evaluation',
 'First sequence: small DeepLog-style embedding32/LSTM64×2, context10, batch256, Adam0.001,10 epochs. This uses trainable event embeddings and mean next-event negative log probability per unit; it is a pilot variant, not exact official DeepLog reproduction. First contextual: masked Transformer128×2,4 heads, context20,15% mask, same batch/lr/epochs; evaluate mean masked-token loss over every position and aggregate within units. This lacks LogBERT’s hypersphere loss and is explicitly not an exact LogBERT replication. The official pinned LogBERT adapter remains a separate implementation task. First faithful semantic LogRobust awaits a pinned fixed word-vector source and attention/BiLSTM adapter; no substitute is silently labelled LogRobust.',
 'Seeds0–4; initially seed0 GT only. Choose epoch by mean normal-validation loss and threshold by validation F1 (ties higher threshold); never test performance. Freeze precision/recall/F1/AP/AUROC/FPR, score direction and unit aggregation. Persist unit scores/labels/IDs, model checkpoint, config hash and validation history. AP/ROC require both test classes. Deterministic seeds and CUBLAS workspace are set. DeepLog short units use zero-left-padded within-unit context and one target, documented as a pilot convention, not an upstream protocol.',
 '## Commands and execution order',
 'CPU inputs are already prepared. After restoring data/cpu_research/ and results_phase3/cpu_research/ from RESULTS_REPO into experiments/, run:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python experiments/log_parsing_gpu_pilot.py smoke\n.venv/bin/python experiments/log_parsing_gpu_pilot.py train --system BGL --condition GT --detector deeplog --seed 0 --device cuda\n```',
 'The train command is the first GPU command. Use the normal GPU-enabled .venv next session; this session’s .venv-cpu has torch+cpu and cannot run CUDA. Install torch with a wheel matching the server driver plus numpy/scipy/scikit-learn if needed; no pretrained model/tokenizer is required. The command never downloads a model. No GPU memory figure was measured; models are small, but peak GPU allocation must be recorded during the first run instead of quoting an unverified GB estimate.',
 'Then run BGL contextual seed0 and HDFS GT controls; inspect validation/data health without altering test splits. Continue seeds1–4 only if the fixed health gate passes. BGL severe temporal OOV drift must be reported by normal/anomaly strata, not used to choose a friendlier test cut. A template-semantic detector may be necessary to distinguish drift from anomalies, but that remains a hypothesis.',
 'Before matched inference: verify complete assignment coverage and original-ID joins, candidate provenance, common unit/label hashes, no cross-split members, normal-only training, train-only vocabulary/IDF and input/target/mask dimensions. CPU smoke passed preprocessing and tiny randomly initialized CPU LSTM/Transformer forward shapes, with no training or smoke performance reported. GPU training/backpropagation and CUDA kernels remain untested.',
 'Resource fallback: lower batch256→64 only for memory failure (record deviation), keep data/splits/architecture/epochs fixed; run seeds serially. Do not overlap GPU parser/model jobs. First GT health uses no LLM inference; defer expensive parser expansion until detector health is useful. Never expand reviews just because representation distances are nonzero.',
 'Expansion requires valid matched outputs, both held-out classes, useful GT health under frozen metrics, and an interpretable GT–parser gap with paired time-block (BGL)/session (HDFS) uncertainty. Compare always-anomaly and UNK-only controls before interpreting sequence gains. Then evaluate stored-style review policies at0/5/10/20/50, keep template-only and membership interventions separate, and charge training/candidate/source labels. Retrained and frozen-detector correction experiments must remain distinct.',
 '## Integration',
 'Available HDFS real AdaParser is exactly GT; BGL real AdaParser changes partitions through two splitGT types and small lexical distortions. Existing frequency/D corrections recover the same stored BGL test lexical features by20 reviews, without a valid anomaly-recovery test. Label-aware U loses substantial line recovery at equal target effort when90 training labels are charged; zero-target U retains some small-budget group recovery but source acquisition is costly. These findings support a feasibility/cost contribution, not a downstream improvement claim. The highest-priority unknown is whether a useful GT detector and an actual parser-induced anomaly-performance gap coexist on the same valid fully covered units.'])
if __name__=='__main__':feasibility();representation();costs();pilot();print('four research reports written')
